        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 4:33PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>At 433 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 10
miles north of Anton Chico, or 19 miles south of Las Vegas, moving
east at 35 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Dilia, Anton Chico, Trujillo, San Agustin, Tecolotito, Los Montoyas
and Chapelle.

This includes the following highways...
Interstate 25 between Mile Markers 333 and 335. State Road 104
between Mile Markers 10 and 34.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to
flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.</instruction>
